          "winningProse": "## Chapter 2: The Taste of Dirt and Salt\n\n### Council Review Scorecard: Chapter 1\n* **Pacing & Hook**: `9.6/10` (Immediate conflict; Kurukshetra into comedic awakening)\n* **Chung Myung Quotient**: `9.8/10` (Unapologetic grumbling; wild tiger grin; dramatic soup whine)\n* **Subtext & Payoff**: `9.3/10` (Bao's neck bruise planted; grandmother's vow introduced)\n* **Overall Council Verdict**: **APPROVED for Publication**.\n\n***\n\nThe first law of martial arts is simple: a sword cannot cut without an arm behind it.\n\nAnd right now, my arm belonged to a fifteen-year-old who got winded pulling up his trousers.\n\n\"One,\" I grunted, pressing my palms against the cold dirt floor.\n\nMy elbows shook. The muscles along my shoulder blades felt like frayed hemp ropes threatening to snap.\n\n\"Two.\"\n\n*Pop.*\n\nA tendon in my right wrist protested with a sharp, burning pinch. My chest hit the dirt with an undignified *thud*, knocking the little wind I had right out of my lungs.\n\nI lay there for three long breaths, my cheek pressed against the packed mud, inhaling the scent of damp earth and old ashes.\n\n\"Pathetic,\" I muttered into the dirt. \"Absolutely, miserably pathetic.\"\n\nTwo push-ups had my heart pounding against my ribs like a trapped sparrow. \n\n*Dantian: empty.*\n*Meridians: rusted solid.*\n*Muscles: thin as dried willow bark.*\n\nIf an enemy from my past life saw me right now, they wouldn't even bother drawing steel. They would die of laughter, and I would be forced to claim victory by default.\n\n\"Jin? What are you doing on the floor?!\"",
